{{also|takk fyri}}
==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{compound|is|takk|fyrir|t1=thanks|t2=for}}, literally meaning “thanks ''for'' ...”. Cognate with {{cog|is|þökk fyrir}} and {{cog|fo|takk fyri}}, ''{{l|fo|tøkk fyri}}''.

===Interjection===
{{head|is|interjection}}

# {{lb|is|with accusative}} [[thank you]], [[thanks]]

====Usage notes====
* The interjection ''{{l|is|takk||thanks}}'' (borrowed from [[w:Danish|Danish]] ''{{l|da|tak}}'', from {{der|is|non|þǫkk}}) is a cognate of ''{{l|is|þökk||a thank, thanks}}'', itself inherited directly from Old Norse.
* The term ''þökk'' is used as a noun, and rarely as an interjection by itself. The derived term ''{{l|is|þökk fyrir}}'' can be used as an interjection.

====Synonyms====
* {{l|is|takk}}
* {{l|is|þökk fyrir}}
* {{l|is|þakka þér}} {{q|singular}} (literally “(I) thank you”)
** {{l|is|þakka þér fyrir}} {{q|singular}} (literally “thank you ''for'' ...”)
** {{l|is|þakka ykkur fyrir}} {{q|plural}} (literally “thank you ''for'' ...”)
* {{l|is|þakka yður}} {{q|singular, formal; rare}} (literally “(I) thank you ...”)
** {{l|is|þakka yður fyrir}} {{q|singular and plural, formal; rare}} (literally “thank you ''for'' ...”)

====Derived terms====
* {{l|is|takk fyrir í dag||thanks for today}}
* {{l|is|takk fyrir í gær||thanks for yesterday}}
* {{l|is|takk fyrir í kvöld||thanks for tonight}}
* {{l|is|takk fyrir mig}} (“thanks for myself”, commonly said to a host for having been received as a guest; both after dining and when departing)
* {{l|is|takk fyrir síðast}}, {{l|is|takk fyrir seinast||thanks for last time}}

====Related terms====
* {{l|is|þakka||to thank}}
* {{l|is|takk kærlega||thank you ''dearly''; thank you very much}}
* {{l|is|kærar þakkir||''dear'' thanks; thank you very much}}
* {{l|is|þúsund þakkir||thousand thanks}}

